# Practice Test

## 1. Display Orders with Product Name

```sql
select o.order_id, o.customer_name, p.product_name 
from products p 
join orders o 
on o.product_id = p.product_id;
```

---

## 2. Show All Products Even if They Were Never Ordered

```sql
select o.order_id, o.customer_name, p.product_name 
from products p 
left join orders o 
on o.product_id = p.product_id;
```

---

## 3. Show Orders Only for Electronics Category

```sql
select o.order_id, o.customer_name, p.product_name 
from orders o 
join products p  
on o.product_id = p.product_id
where p.category='Electronics';
```

---

## 4. Show All Orders Sorted by Product Price (High to Low)

```sql
select o.order_id, o.customer_name, p.product_name, p.price 
from products p 
join orders o 
on o.product_id = p.product_id
order by p.price DESC;
```

---

## 5. Show Number of Orders for Each Product

```sql
select p.product_name, count(o.order_id) as no_of_orders 
from products p 
left join orders o 
on o.product_id = p.product_id
group by p.product_name;
```

---

## 6. Show Total Earned Revenue Per Product in Descending Order

```sql
select p.product_name, sum(o.quantity*p.price) as total 
from products p 
join orders o 
on o.product_id = p.product_id
group by p.product_name
order by sum(o.quantity*p.price) DESC;
```

---

## 7. Show Products Whose Total Revenue is Greater Than 2000

```sql
select p.product_name, sum(o.quantity*p.price) as total 
from products p 
join orders o 
on o.product_id = p.product_id
group by p.product_name
having sum(o.quantity*p.price)>2000;
```

---

## 8. Show Unique Customers Who Ordered Fitness Products

```sql
select distinct o.order_id, o.customer_name 
from products p 
join orders o 
on o.product_id = p.product_id
where p.category='Fitness';
```